module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.LongExactSequence.AllModules
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.SectionsIso.Restriction
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.VanishingTFAE.ClopenVanishing

/-!
# A clopen zero locus is exactly cohomological dimension zero

Let `I` be a finitely generated ideal of a commutative ring `A` and `Y = V(I)` its zero locus in
`Spec A`. This file proves

  `H^i_Y(A) = 0 for every i > 0  ↔  Y is open and closed`,

which is the equivalence **(1) ⇔ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0DX7] at `d = 0`**.

The implication from right to left is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.isZero_localCohomologyModule_of_isClopen_zeroLocus`, proved in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.VanishingTFAE.ClopenVanishing`. What is proved here is the
other one, and it is proved **algebraically**, not along the route of the source.

The source deduces openness of `Y` by showing that `U = Spec A \ Y` is affine — Serre's criterion
applied to the vanishing of `H^1(U, F)` for quasi-coherent `F` — and then that `U ⟶ Spec A` is a
closed immersion. That route needs the comparison between the sheaf cohomology of `U` and the
local cohomology of `A` in degree one, which this library does not have. The route taken instead
produces the idempotent directly:

* vanishing of `H^1_Y(J)` for the ideal `J = I`, read off the long exact sequence of
  `0 ⟶ I ⟶ A ⟶ A/I ⟶ 0`, makes the `I`-power-torsion submodule of `A` surject onto `A/I`. In
  elements: there is `a ∈ A` with `1 - a ∈ I` and `f^n a = 0` for every generator `f` of `I`.
* `y = 1 - a` then satisfies `z y = z` for every `z` in the ideal `K` generated by the `n`-th
  powers of the generators, because `z a = 0`; and `y` lies in the radical of `K`, so some
  `t = y^m` lies in `K`. That `t` is idempotent, since `t y = t` iterates to `t y^m = t`, and
  `V(I) = V(t)` because `K ≤ (t) ≤ I ≤ √K`.

The first step is carried out in the Čech model of local cohomology
(`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.CechModel`) rather than in the derived category. That is
forced: the identification of local cohomology with Čech cohomology is available only as a
`Nonempty` isomorphism, with no naturality in the module, so a statement about a *map* of local
cohomology modules cannot be transported across it. Inside the Čech model everything needed is
available — the Čech complexes of a short exact sequence of modules form a short exact sequence of
complexes
(`Stacks.LocalCohomology.LongExactSequence.shortExact_map_cechTerm`), the differentials are
natural in the module, and the degree-zero and degree-one terms have explicit coordinates — and
only *vanishing* has to cross between the two models, which needs no naturality.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_sub_one_mem_and_pow_mul_eq_zero` — the element-level consequence
  of the vanishing: an element congruent to `1` modulo `I` that every generator of `I` kills a
  power of.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isClopen_zeroLocus_of_isZero_localCohomologyModule` — **(1) ⇒ (3) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0DX7] at `d = 0`**.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isClopen_zeroLocus_iff_isZero_localCohomologyModule` — the two
  directions together, which is **(1) ⇔ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0DX7] at `d = 0`**.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isClopen_zeroLocus_iff_cohomologicalDimension_le_zero` — the same
  equivalence read on the cohomological dimension of Tag 0DX8.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks]` attribute is placed. The tagged statement of Tag 0DX7 is a three-way equivalence
for an arbitrary `d ≥ -1`; what is proved here is one of its three clauses at one value of `d`.
The assembled equivalence at `-1 ≤ d ≤ 0` is
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.VanishingTFAE.LowBoundTFAE`.

`HasDerivedCategory.standard` is pinned as a local instance, as it is in every file of this
development; it is already baked into the type of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyModule`. Nothing below mentions a coproduct of a derived
category, which is the situation in which the standard model would make a statement vacuous.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DX7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DX7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DX8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DX8)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-! ### Two elementary tools -/

/-- A fraction of a localized module vanishes only if some element of the multiplicative system
kills its numerator. -/
theorem exists_smul_eq_zero_of_mk_eq_zero {S : Submonoid A} {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module A M] {m : M} {s : S} (h : LocalizedModule.mk m s = 0) :
    ∃ t : A, t ∈ S ∧ t • m = 0 := by
  rw [show (0 : LocalizedModule S M) = LocalizedModule.mk 0 1 from
    (LocalizedModule.zero_mk 1).symm, LocalizedModule.mk_eq] at h
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := h
  exact ⟨u, u.2, by simpa [Submonoid.smul_def] using hu⟩

/-- **Vanishing of `Ȟ¹` of the Čech complex, in elements.** A degree-one Čech cocycle is a
coboundary. -/
theorem exists_cechD_zero_eq_of_isZero_homology_one {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A) (N : Type u)
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] (h₁ : IsZero ((Cech.cechComplex f N).homology 1))
    (x : Cech.cechTerm f N 1) (hx : Cech.cechD f N 1 x = 0) :
    ∃ y : Cech.cechTerm f N 0, Cech.cechD f N 0 y = x := by
  have hE : (HomologicalComplex.sc' (Cech.cechComplex f N) 0 1 2).Exact := by
    rw [← HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff' _ 0 1 2 (by simp) (by simp)]
    exact (HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff_isZero_homology _ 1).2 h₁
  have key : ∀ x : Cech.cechTerm f N 1,
      (ConcreteCategory.hom ((Cech.cechComplex f N).d 1 2)) x = 0 →
      ∃ y : Cech.cechTerm f N 0, (ConcreteCategory.hom ((Cech.cechComplex f N).d 0 1)) y = x :=
    (ShortComplex.moduleCat_exact_iff _).1 hE
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := key x (by
    rw [show ConcreteCategory.hom ((Cech.cechComplex f N).d 1 2) = Cech.cechD f N 1 from
      LongExactSequence.cechComplex_d_hom f 1]
    exact hx)
  refine ⟨y, ?_⟩
  rw [show ConcreteCategory.hom ((Cech.cechComplex f N).d 0 1) = Cech.cechD f N 0 from
    LongExactSequence.cechComplex_d_hom f 0] at hy
  exact hy

/-- **The degree-zero identification of the Čech complex is natural in the module.** Both sides
are the constant fraction `g m / 1` on the empty index set. -/
theorem cechTermLinearMap_zero_cechTermZeroEquiv_symm {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (M N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (g : M ⟶ N) (m : M) :
    cechTermLinearMap f g.hom 0 ((cechTermZeroEquiv f M).symm m) =
      (cechTermZeroEquiv f N).symm (g m) := by
  rw [cechTermZeroEquiv_symm_apply, cechTermZeroEquiv_symm_apply,
    cechTermLinearMap, DirectSum.lmap_lof]
  congr 1
  exact localizedModuleMap_mk _ _ _ _

/-! ### The element produced by the vanishing -/

/-- **The `I`-power-torsion submodule of `A` surjects onto `A/I`**, in elements: if the local
cohomology of `A` with support in `V(I)` vanishes in every positive degree, then there is `a ∈ A`
congruent to `1` modulo `I` which the `n`-th power of every generator of `I` annihilates.

The vanishing hypothesis is first propagated from `A` to every module by
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.isZero_homology_localCohomology_of_isZero_homology_self`, and applied to
the ideal `I` itself in degree one. The chase then runs inside the Čech model, where `0 ⟶ I ⟶ A ⟶
A/I ⟶ 0` gives a short exact sequence of Čech complexes: the coboundary of `1 ∈ A` dies in the
Čech complex of `A/I`, because each of its coordinates is the fraction `1/1` in a localization of
`A/I` at a generator of `I`, which `I` kills; so it comes from a degree-one cochain of `I`, which
is a cocycle because its image is one, hence a coboundary by the vanishing of `Ȟ¹`; and
subtracting that coboundary from `1` leaves the required element. -/
theorem exists_sub_one_mem_and_pow_mul_eq_zero {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A) (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG)
    (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I)
    (h : ∀ i : ℤ, 0 < i → IsZero (localCohomologyModule A I hI (ModuleCat.of A A) i)) :
    ∃ (a : A) (n : ℕ), 1 - a ∈ I ∧ ∀ i, f i ^ n * a = 0 := by
  classical
  have hfmem : ∀ i, f i ∈ I := fun i => by
    rw [← hIf]; exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  set S := (Submodule.mkQ I).shortComplexKer with hSdef
  have hS : S.ShortExact := LinearMap.shortExact_shortComplexKer (Submodule.mkQ_surjective I)
  have hall : ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i : ℤ), 0 < i →
      IsZero (localCohomologyModule A I hI M i) :=
    fun M i hi => isZero_homology_localCohomology_of_isZero_homology_self.{u} I hI 0 h M i hi
  have h₁ : IsZero ((Cech.cechComplex f (S.X₁ : Type _)).homology 1) := by
    refine IsZero.of_iso ?_ (HomologicalComplex.extendHomologyIso
      (Cech.cechComplex f (S.X₁ : Type _)) ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat
      (j := 1) (j' := (1 : ℤ)) (by simp)).symm
    exact (isZero_cechHomology_iff_isZero_homology_localCohomology f I hI hIf S.X₁ 1).2
      (hall S.X₁ 1 one_pos)
  have hexact₁ : Function.Exact (cechTermMap f S.f 1)
      (cechTermMap f S.g 1) :=
    (ShortComplex.ShortExact.moduleCat_exact_iff_function_exact _).1
      (LongExactSequence.shortExact_map_cechTerm f S hS 1).exact
  have hinj₂ : Function.Injective (cechTermMap f S.f 2) :=
    (LongExactSequence.shortExact_map_cechTerm f S hS 2).injective_f
  have hpow : ∀ i, Cech.cechSub f ({i} : Finset (Fin r)) = Submonoid.powers (f i) := fun i => by
    simp [Cech.cechSub]
  set one₀ : Cech.cechTerm f (S.X₂ : Type _) 0 :=
    (cechTermZeroEquiv f S.X₂).symm (1 : A) with hone₀
  set z₀ : Cech.cechTerm f (S.X₂ : Type _) 1 := Cech.cechD f (S.X₂ : Type _) 0 one₀ with hz₀
  -- the coboundary of `1` vanishes in the Čech complex of `A/I`
  have hz₀g : cechTermMap f S.g 1 z₀ = 0 := by
    rw [LongExactSequence.cechTermMap_eq_cechTermLinearMap, hz₀,
      cechTermLinearMap_cechD, cechTermLinearMap_zero_cechTermZeroEquiv_symm]
    refine (cechTermOneEquiv f S.X₃).injective ?_
    rw [map_zero]
    funext i
    show (cechTermOneEquiv f S.X₃) _ i = (0 : Cech.cechMod f (S.X₃ : Type _) {i})
    rw [cechTermOneEquiv_cechD_zero]
    rw [show (LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap (Cech.cechSub f {i}) (S.X₃ : Type _)) (S.g 1) =
        LocalizedModule.mk (S.g (1 : A)) 1 from rfl,
      show (0 : Cech.cechMod f (S.X₃ : Type _) {i}) = LocalizedModule.mk 0 1 from
        (LocalizedModule.zero_mk 1).symm, LocalizedModule.mk_eq]
    refine ⟨⟨f i, by rw [hpow]; exact Submonoid.mem_powers _⟩, ?_⟩
    simp only [one_smul, smul_zero, Submonoid.smul_def]
    show Submodule.mkQ I (f i * 1) = 0
    rw [mul_one, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
    exact hfmem i
  -- so it comes from a degree-one cochain of `I`, which is a cocycle, hence a coboundary
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (hexact₁ z₀).1 hz₀g
  have hdz : Cech.cechD f (S.X₁ : Type _) 1 z = 0 := by
    apply hinj₂
    rw [map_zero, LongExactSequence.cechTermMap_eq_cechTermLinearMap,
      cechTermLinearMap_cechD,
      ← LongExactSequence.cechTermMap_eq_cechTermLinearMap, hz, hz₀, ← LinearMap.comp_apply,
      Cech.cechD_comp_cechD]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_cechD_zero_eq_of_isZero_homology_one f (S.X₁ : Type _) h₁ z hdz
  set wA : (S.X₁ : Type _) := cechTermZeroEquiv f S.X₁ w with hwA
  have hnat : (cechTermZeroEquiv f S.X₂).symm (S.f wA) =
      cechTermLinearMap f S.f.hom 0 w := by
    rw [← cechTermLinearMap_zero_cechTermZeroEquiv_symm f S.X₁ S.X₂ S.f wA, hwA,
      LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  have hdw : Cech.cechD f (S.X₂ : Type _) 0
      (cechTermLinearMap f S.f.hom 0 w) = z₀ := by
    rw [← cechTermLinearMap_cechD,
      ← LongExactSequence.cechTermMap_eq_cechTermLinearMap, hw, hz]
  have hkey : Cech.cechD f (S.X₂ : Type _) 0
      ((cechTermZeroEquiv f S.X₂).symm (1 - S.f wA)) = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, map_sub, hnat, hdw, ← hone₀, ← hz₀, sub_self]
  -- reading the coordinates of that cocycle gives the annihilation
  have hvan : ∀ i, ∃ k : ℕ, f i ^ k * (1 - S.f wA) = 0 := by
    intro i
    have hco : (cechTermOneEquiv f S.X₂)
        (Cech.cechD f (S.X₂ : Type _) 0 ((cechTermZeroEquiv f S.X₂).symm (1 - S.f wA))) i =
        (0 : Cech.cechMod f (S.X₂ : Type _) {i}) := by
      rw [hkey, map_zero]; rfl
    rw [cechTermOneEquiv_cechD_zero] at hco
    obtain ⟨t, ht, hta⟩ := exists_smul_eq_zero_of_mk_eq_zero
      (S := Cech.cechSub f ({i} : Finset (Fin r))) (s := 1) hco
    rw [hpow i, Submonoid.mem_powers_iff] at ht
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := ht
    exact ⟨k, by rw [hk]; simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hta⟩
  choose k hk using hvan
  refine ⟨1 - S.f wA, Finset.univ.sup k, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hmem : ((wA : A)) ∈ I := by
      have h₂ := wA.2
      simpa [Submodule.ker_mkQ] using h₂
    rw [sub_sub_cancel]
    exact hmem
  · intro i
    have hle : k i ≤ Finset.univ.sup k := Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ i)
    rw [show Finset.univ.sup k = k i + (Finset.univ.sup k - k i) by omega, pow_add, mul_assoc,
      mul_comm (f i ^ (Finset.univ.sup k - k i)), ← mul_assoc, hk i, zero_mul]

/-! ### From the element to the idempotent -/

/-- **The element produces an idempotent cutting out the same zero locus.** Given `a` congruent to
`1` modulo `I` which the `n`-th power of every generator annihilates, `V(I)` is open and closed.

Let `K` be the ideal generated by the `n`-th powers of the generators, so that `z a = 0` for every
`z ∈ K`, and let `y = 1 - a ∈ I`; then `z y = z` for every `z ∈ K`. Each generator lies in the
radical of `K`, hence so does `y`, so `t = y ^ m` lies in `K` for some `m ≥ 1`. Iterating `z y = z`
gives `z = z t` for every `z ∈ K`, which both makes `t` idempotent (`t ∈ K`) and shows
`K ≤ (t)`; and `(t) ≤ I ≤ √K`, so `V(I) = V(t)`. -/
theorem isClopen_zeroLocus_of_exists_sub_one_mem {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A) (I : Ideal A)
    (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I) (a : A) (n : ℕ)
    (ha : 1 - a ∈ I) (hn : ∀ i, f i ^ n * a = 0) :
    IsClopen (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A)) := by
  set K := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => f i ^ n) with hK
  have hKa : ∀ z ∈ K, z * a = 0 := by
    intro z hz
    induction hz using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx => obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hx; exact hn i
    | zero => exact zero_mul a
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [add_mul, hx, hy, add_zero]
    | smul c x _ hx => rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_assoc, hx, mul_zero]
  set y := 1 - a with hy
  have hfix : ∀ z ∈ K, z * y = z := fun z hz => by
    rw [hy, mul_sub, mul_one, hKa z hz, sub_zero]
  have hIrad : I ≤ K.radical := by
    rw [← hIf, Ideal.span_le]
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact ⟨n, Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hIrad ha
  set t := y ^ (m + 1) with ht
  have htK : t ∈ K := by rw [ht, pow_succ]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hm
  have hpowfix : ∀ z ∈ K, ∀ j : ℕ, z * y ^ j = z := by
    intro z hz j
    induction j with
    | zero => rw [pow_zero, mul_one]
    | succ j ih => rw [pow_succ, ← mul_assoc, ih, hfix z hz]
  have hidem : IsIdempotentElem t := by
    show t * t = t
    rw [ht]
    exact hpowfix _ htK (m + 1)
  have hKt : K ≤ Ideal.span {t} := by
    intro z hz
    rw [Ideal.mem_span_singleton']
    exact ⟨z, hpowfix z hz (m + 1)⟩
  have htI : Ideal.span {t} ≤ I := by
    rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact ht ▸ Ideal.pow_mem_of_mem I ha _ (Nat.succ_pos m)
  have heq : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Ideal.span {t} : Set A) := by
    refine subset_antisymm (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_anti_mono_ideal htI) ?_
    refine subset_trans (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_anti_mono_ideal hKt) ?_
    rw [← PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_radical]
    exact PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_anti_mono_ideal hIrad
  rw [heq]
  exact isClopen_zeroLocus_span_singleton_of_isIdempotentElem hidem

/-! ### The criterion -/

/-- **(1) ⇒ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0DX7] at `d = 0`.** If the local cohomology of `A` with support in
`V(I)` vanishes in every positive degree, then `V(I)` is open and closed. -/
theorem isClopen_zeroLocus_of_isZero_localCohomologyModule (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG)
    (h : ∀ i : ℤ, 0 < i → IsZero (localCohomologyModule A I hI (ModuleCat.of A A) i)) :
    IsClopen (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A)) := by
  obtain ⟨r, f, hf⟩ := Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.1 hI
  obtain ⟨a, n, ha, hn⟩ := exists_sub_one_mem_and_pow_mul_eq_zero f I hI hf h
  exact isClopen_zeroLocus_of_exists_sub_one_mem f I hf a n ha hn

/-- **(1) ⇔ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0DX7] at `d = 0`.** For a finitely generated ideal `I` of `A` the
local cohomology `H^i_{V(I)}(A)` vanishes for every `i > 0` exactly when `V(I)` is open and
closed. -/
theorem isClopen_zeroLocus_iff_isZero_localCohomologyModule (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG) :
    (∀ i : ℤ, 0 < i → IsZero (localCohomologyModule A I hI (ModuleCat.of A A) i)) ↔
      IsClopen (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A)) :=
  ⟨isClopen_zeroLocus_of_isZero_localCohomologyModule I hI,
    fun h i hi => isZero_localCohomologyModule_of_isClopen_zeroLocus.{u} I hI h _ i hi⟩

/-- **A clopen zero locus is exactly cohomological dimension at most zero.** The cohomological
dimension of Tag 0DX8 is `≤ 0` precisely when `V(I)` is open and closed. -/
theorem isClopen_zeroLocus_iff_cohomologicalDimension_le_zero (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG) :
    cohomologicalDimension A I hI ≤ 0 ↔ IsClopen (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A)) := by
  refine ⟨fun h => (isClopen_zeroLocus_iff_isZero_localCohomologyModule I hI).1 fun i hi => ?_,
    cohomologicalDimension_le_zero_of_isClopen_zeroLocus A I hI⟩
  exact (isLocalCohomologyBound_cohomologicalDimension A I hI).2 i (lt_of_le_of_lt h hi)

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

end
